{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MtlsEndpointAliases","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A TLS listener decides whether to request a client certificate during the handshake,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before it has seen any HTTP, so “ask for a certificate on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/oauth2\/token"},{"text":" but not on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/oauth2\/authorize"},{"text":"” is not something one listener can do. A deployment wanting both runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two, and this object names the second.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only these seven are ever aliased. ","type":"text"},{"code":"authorization_endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"end_session_endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"front-channel and ","type":"text"},{"code":"jwks_uri","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is public key material, so §21.3 rule 2 forbids synthesising","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an alias for any of them — sending a browser to an mTLS host raises a native","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"certificate-chooser dialog most users cannot answer. ","type":"text"},{"code":"issuer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not an endpoint and does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not move either: §12.4 rule 3 still compares ","type":"text"},{"code":"iss","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against it by exact string.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every property is optional","type":"text"}]},{"text":", though the server’s schema marks them required. AXIAM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds them from one path through a shared macro and so always publishes the complete set,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but RFC 8705 §5 permits an OP to alias fewer, and the shape of this member must never be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"why a client stops working — the same principle rule 2 point 1 states for the object as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whole, one level in. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" entry falls back to the top-level endpoint of the same name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly as an absent object does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/MtlsEndpointAliases"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/mtlsendpointaliases"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"RFC 8705 §5 ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mtls_endpoint_aliases"},{"text":" — the seven endpoints re-based on the host that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"performs the mutual-TLS handshake (wire schema ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MtlsEndpointAliases"},{"text":", contract 1.40; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seventh, CIBA’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backchannel_authentication_endpoint"},{"text":", joined in contract 1.58).","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK19MtlsEndpointAliasesV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MtlsEndpointAliases"}],"title":"MtlsEndpointAliases","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text"